# Recorded eval runs — integrity anchor for the claim-support rollout.
#
# release_release-1.jsonl is the 66-answer release run of 2026-08-19 and is the
# baseline every later --compare is measured against. It cannot be rebuilt: a
# re-run calls the model 66 more times and is a different sample. Verify before
# trusting any number derived from these files, and after any git operation
# that touched data/eval/:
#
#     sha256sum -c data/eval/CHECKSUMS.sha256      # run from the repo root
#
# Regenerate ONLY when deliberately adding a new recorded run:
#     sha256sum data/eval/release_*.jsonl data/eval/answers_baseline_*.jsonl
#
574a2b0d043a726a7b4e13794d957a5932b4e9d0195843b31c1c64c4bad0ae45  data/eval/release_release-1.jsonl
da75da447aee66bb441ec975093a94577388f392c38ba1bfb05f17f3f4ac3c0a  data/eval/answers_baseline_baseline-sample-v2.jsonl
a61f5aabd4675058de22131dad71682ccc082d62f3ff3ecac0ba692b6c01c045  data/eval/answers_baseline_retrieval-all-v2.jsonl
73a1d6f807b536dc9dc3427f0262cb0a056218426936a36b662f12fe921905a4  data/eval/answers_baseline_retrieval-scoped-ab.jsonl
ce0463faef872918bd3d85078135ba9ab4d187eea223ffffdeca26435a9b9228  data/eval/answers_baseline_step1-sample.jsonl
#
# The corpus fact registry, added in Wave 2. It is an INPUT to rag/verify.py —
# every conflict verdict, every registry-backed figure and every 'report both
# figures' suppression reads it — so an absent or edited registry changes every
# number derived from the verifier. It was git-ignored under `data/**` until
# Wave 2 tracked it with a negative pattern; these lines are what makes a
# silent edit fail instead of re-scoring a different system. Paths are relative
# to the repo root, same as the lines above.
559a3318fb6db8360ef6159dc00e29882cf829670925bf91f4659b2a8f665b4f  data/registry.json
3476e554a31c8dcdc81a71a4a75d0033780b5493f53263b51def6593eaea8b53  data/registry_v2.json
